* Two-Transistor Fuzz — exported from Lutherie
* Two directly coupled transistors with feedback bias through R3. Fuzz sets how much emitter degeneration is bypassed.

Vsig SIGSRC 0 SIN(0 0.3 220.0) AC 1
Rsig SIGSRC IN 1k
CC1 IN N2 2.2u
QQ1 N3 N2 0 Q_BC109
RR1 VCC_9V N3 33k
VVCC1 VCC_9V 0 DC 9.0
QQ2 N5 N3 N6 Q_BC109
RR2 VCC_9V N5 8.2k
* Fuzz pot 1k B taper at 80%
RVR1a 0 N7 800
RVR1b N7 N6 200
CC2 0 N7 22u
RR3 N2 N6 100k
CC3 N5 N8 10n
* Volume pot 500k A taper at 50%
RVR2a 0 OUT 50k
RVR2b OUT N8 450k
Rload OUT 0 1Meg

.model Q_BC109 NPN(Is=1.8e-14 Bf=400.0 Br=35.5 Vaf=80.0 Nf=1.0 Cje=8e-12 Cjc=4e-12 Mje=0 Mjc=0)

.options reltol=1e-5 abstol=1e-13 vntol=1e-8 method=trap
.tran 1.3020833333333333e-06 0.3 0 1.3020833333333333e-06
.control
set wr_singlescale
set numdgt=12
run
wrdata two_transistor_fuzz.ngspice.txt v(OUT)
.endc
.end